<title>USA: Halifax wins case in Virginia's top court.</title>
<headline>Halifax wins case in Virginia's top court.</headline>
<dateline>ALEXANDRIA, Va. 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Halifax Corp, a technology and facilities services company, said Monday that the Supreme Court of Virginia affirmed a trial court's verdict in its favor.</p>
<p>The verdict had been appealed by plaintiff Commercial Business Systems Inc, which had accused Halifax of interfering with business expected from BellSouth Corp.</p>
<p>After a jury trial in 1995, the plaintiff was awarded damages of $435,000, which a trial judge later reversed, according to Halifax.</p>
